weewx-carbonsteel-series

v1.0.0  (30 September 2026)
*   First release under the name weewx-carbonsteel-series (previously
    developed as weewx-steelseries v3). Extension, report and options section
    CarbonSteelSeries; service user.carbonsteelseries.CarbonSteelSeriesRealtime
    configured in [CarbonSteelSeriesRealtime]. Skin and page folder 'CS'.
*   Installing over a pre-release build ('SteelSeries', or an early v1.0.0 in
    the 'ss' folder) carries its settings across automatically.
*   Optional gauges page for the Seasons skin (carbonsteel-gauges.html):
    Seasons title bar, stylesheet and wording, sharing the CS page's settings
    and data. Adds one file to the Seasons folder (plus the title-bar button
    below). The installer asks whether to add it (or pass --seasons=y|n).
*   Optional gauges page for the Belchertown-new skin (carbonsteel/): generated
    by Belchertown's own report, with its header, menu, theme switch and
    footer; gauges shown as Belchertown-style cards that follow its light/dark
    mode. Adds one template and two weewx.conf entries, both removed on
    uninstall, plus the menu item below. The installer asks whether to add it (or pass --belchertown=y|n).
*   "Live Gauges" links in the host skins' headers so visitors can find the
    pages: a button beside RSS in the Seasons title bar (titlebar.inc) and an
    item in the Belchertown menu (nav-menu-custom.inc, created from its example
    if missing). Each is a marked block that only shows while its page is
    installed; answering no removes it, and re-running never duplicates it.
*   The Seasons and Belchertown pages leave out the CarbonSteel header (outlook
    ticker, update counter, face/bezel/units switches): the host skin's own
    header, theme and units apply. Seasons: always light, in the units of the
    Seasons report. Belchertown: follows its light/dark mode and its units,
    including its unit switcher (unit_switching = 1) as the visitor changes it.
*   Belchertown page: when Belchertown shows live data over MQTT
    (mqtt_websockets_enabled = 1), the gauges take their current readings from
    the same broker and topic; realtime.json still supplies the day's figures
    (read once a minute while MQTT is live) and takes over at once if MQTT
    stops. Reads weewx-mqtt packets in any unit system.
*   Styles split into gauges.css (page) and components.css (gauges); embed.css
    scopes the components for pages inside other skins.
*   Independent of the original SteelSeries Weather Gauges skin: separate
    report, skin folder, web folder, live data file and visitor settings, so
    both can be installed on the same station.
*   Complete rewrite for WeeWX 5 and Python 3.9-3.13 (tested on WeeWX 5.5.2,
    Python 3.13.7). Installs with `weectl extension install`.
*   Realtime service writes realtime.json on every LOOP packet: current values,
    today's highs/lows seeded from daily summaries, rain day/hour/24h/month/year,
    10-minute wind average, gust and direction range, wind rose, 3-hour
    pressure tendency.
*   Vector SVG gauges drawn with D3 v7, in the style of the original SteelSeries
    gauges: chrome or black-metal bezel; beige, white, anthracite or carbon-fibre
    face; light/dark themes; visitor-selectable face, bezel and units.
*   Header with station coordinates, status LED, Open-Meteo outlook ticker and
    seconds-since-update counter.
*   Optional 24-hour sparklines and detail charts, and a Year at a glance
    calendar heat-map; the installer asks whether to show each
    (or pass --sparklines=y|n --calendar=y|n).
*   Licensed GPL v3 or later.

History of the original weewx-steelseries extension (Gary Roderick), on which
this project was originally based:

v2.6.3
*   upgraded to SteelSeries Weather Gauges v2.6.3
v2.6.1
